WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:05.200
Hello and welcome to this video on jump animations.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:14.519
In this video we are going to be using the state machine to create a jump animation loop.

3
00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:17.519
That's going to consist of three animations.

4
00:00:17.519 --> 00:00:23.940
So it's going to consist of start jump, a falling loop, and a landing animation.

5
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:29.460
So let's go back into the project now.

6
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.460
So the first thing we're going to want to do is open back up our animation blueprint.

7
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:44.469
Now in order to trigger this animation we need to know if the character is in the air.

8
00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:48.469
So this would cover either if it was falling or jumping.

9
00:00:48.469 --> 00:00:53.429
And we're going to do that on the event blueprint update animation.

10
00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:59.619
Now the first thing I'm going to do is I'm going to add in the sequence at the beginning.

11
00:00:59.619 --> 00:01:05.620
And I can do that by holding down the S key and left clicking on the background.

12
00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:09.170
I'm just going to connect that up here.

13
00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.519
This is just so I can keep things tidy really.

14
00:01:12.519 --> 00:01:24.420
And here on the then1 output pin, what I'm going to do is I'm going to grab another reference to the character movement.

15
00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.420
So I'll just copy this and paste this here.

16
00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:33.560
Because we're going to use the character movement component again.

17
00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.560
Because that's going to tell us if we are in the air.

18
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.040
There's a function which allows us to figure this out.

19
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.069
You drag off and you type in isFalling.

20
00:01:45.069 --> 00:01:55.260
And you'll see that this function will detect if you are falling.

21
00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:02.260
And it's going to return a boolean value for true if you're falling and false if you're not falling.

22
00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:08.060
So I will right-hand click on this and promote this to a variable.

23
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:16.449
And I'm going to call this variable isFalling.

24
00:02:16.449 --> 00:02:21.169
And connect that up.

25
00:02:21.169 --> 00:02:25.969
All this is going to do each time the animation is updated,

26
00:02:25.969 --> 00:02:30.969
is just going to check the character movement, see if we're falling and save that to a variable.

27
00:02:30.969 --> 00:02:37.020
As I mentioned before, this is going to run multiple animations.

28
00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:40.020
And we're going to use the state machine to achieve this.

29
00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:44.090
So I'm going to jump back into our locomotion state machine.

30
00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:49.439
And as you can see, at the moment, we only have idle to run.

31
00:02:49.439 --> 00:02:54.400
Now, I want to add three more states.

32
00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:02.620
And I'm going to do that by just coming over to my asset library here.

33
00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.620
And I'm going to search for jump.

34
00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:11.490
And I'll find mm underscore jump, drag that in.

35
00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:20.620
You can see it's going to automatically create a state that is going to play the mm underscore jump animation.

36
00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:23.620
It's a nice quick way to make a state.

37
00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.620
I could rename it, but I'm not going to worry about that now.

38
00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:34.639
The next one I want, if I type in full, is the mm underscore full loop.

39
00:03:34.639 --> 00:03:37.930
Drag that in, place that over here.

40
00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:42.780
And the final one I want is land.

41
00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.580
And I'm going to drag that in down the bottom here.

42
00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:55.020
Now, in order for us to use any of these, we are going to have to connect them up.

43
00:03:55.020 --> 00:04:00.139
So if I come from the idle to run, drag over and connect that up,

44
00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:05.139
it's going to create me a transition between these two states.

45
00:04:05.139 --> 00:04:06.689
Do that.

46
00:04:06.689 --> 00:04:12.689
And I am going to create another transition from the jump to the full loop.

47
00:04:12.689 --> 00:04:17.100
The last one from the full loop to the land loop.

48
00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:21.100
And the final one back to the idle to run.

49
00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:26.670
Now this is the first time we've come across transitions.

50
00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:31.670
The transition is going to be a gate which, when the condition is true,

51
00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:37.670
it will move you into the other state or animation with a little bit of a blend in between.

52
00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:42.860
So at the moment, if I was to click on the idle to run animation,

53
00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:48.860
you can see here I have a boolean input with a can enter transition.

54
00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:51.930
Now we have nothing plugged into this.

55
00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:57.930
We want to plug in some kind of condition to see if we can enter this transition.

56
00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:05.220
And what we're going to do for that is we're just going to grab the isFalling variable that we populated

57
00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.250
and place that on top of it.

58
00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.250
So if I jump back,

59
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:15.250
so what this is going to mean is we're going to start in the idle to run.

60
00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:19.439
And as soon as it's detected that we're falling,

61
00:05:19.439 --> 00:05:27.600
it's going to move down this transition to the mm underscore jump and play that animation.

62
00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:34.560
Now we also want to move out of this transition into the m underscore m full loop.

63
00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:39.810
So if I double click on this transition and to enter this transition,

64
00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:45.810
I want to wait until the animation that we've just played is almost finished.

65
00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:49.810
So how I'm going to do that is I'm going to right-hand click

66
00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:53.810
and I am going to search for remain.

67
00:05:53.810 --> 00:06:00.540
And you'll see that we have an option of time remaining and time remaining ratio.

68
00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:03.540
I'm going to use the time remaining ratio

69
00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:16.310
and I'm going to drag out and I'm going to do is less than and have 0.1

70
00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:20.310
less than 0.1. So right at the end of the animation.

71
00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:25.350
Now I'm going to connect that up.

72
00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:32.769
This means when the animation is almost over, you can enter the transition into the next section.

73
00:06:32.769 --> 00:06:39.660
Now we're in the full loop.

74
00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:44.949
I want to leave the full loop when we're no longer falling.

75
00:06:44.949 --> 00:06:48.949
So it's going to remain in here until we hit the ground.

76
00:06:48.949 --> 00:06:53.079
And so I'm going to jump into this transition here.

77
00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:57.980
From here, again, I'm going to grab the is falling.

78
00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:04.139
However, this time I'm just going to get it because I want to do this one on the floor.

79
00:07:04.139 --> 00:07:08.139
So I want to add a boolean for not.

80
00:07:08.139 --> 00:07:12.139
A not boolean and I want to plug that in.

81
00:07:12.139 --> 00:07:17.680
So all this is going to do is it's going to check that we are no longer falling.

82
00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.680
Then it will allow us to enter the next state.

83
00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:26.060
Finally, for our last transition, I'm going to jump in.

84
00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:30.629
We are just going to kick this arm.

85
00:07:30.629 --> 00:07:35.629
So this means we will automatically be able to enter the other transition.

86
00:07:35.629 --> 00:07:38.790
So we're going to do this because this animation is so short

87
00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:44.790
that just the blend in and the blend out time is going to be enough for us.

88
00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:48.709
Hit compile.

89
00:07:48.709 --> 00:07:52.709
And now if I come back into the game and I play,

90
00:07:52.709 --> 00:07:55.709
you're going to see that we hit something a little bit odd.

91
00:07:55.709 --> 00:08:03.569
If I jump, suddenly at a small point, I shrink down to almost nothing.

92
00:08:03.569 --> 00:08:07.569
Now this is an oddity of the land animation.

93
00:08:09.459 --> 00:08:13.509
So let's go back to the stage tree.

94
00:08:13.509 --> 00:08:16.509
If I go into the mm underscore land.

95
00:08:16.509 --> 00:08:23.740
Now the odd thing about the land animation is this is an additive animation.

96
00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:27.740
So it is actually very small because it only contains the data

97
00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.740
that would need to be added to another animation

98
00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:36.740
in order to imitate the rebound on the floor.

99
00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.960
So therefore, if we play this as a simple animation,

100
00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:46.470
it's going to shrink the character down to that small additive data.

101
00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:50.470
Now, in order to fix this, what I'm going to do is

102
00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:55.470
I am going to disconnect the result pin here.

103
00:08:55.470 --> 00:09:01.879
And I'm going to search for a apply additive.

104
00:09:01.879 --> 00:09:07.120
I'm going to plug this into our output pin.

105
00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:12.440
I'm going to plug the mm underscore land into the additive.

106
00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:16.440
Now I need a base animation at this point to play.

107
00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:19.570
So we're going to use the blend space that we created.

108
00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:22.570
So I'm going to find the my blend space walk run,

109
00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:27.570
drag that in, and then plug that into the base.

110
00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:33.629
And again, in order to get this to work, we need to add the speed in.

111
00:09:33.629 --> 00:09:38.879
And so what this is going to do is it's going to go back to our walk cycle and play that

112
00:09:38.879 --> 00:09:40.879
because we've hit the ground.

113
00:09:40.879 --> 00:09:45.879
And it's just going to add in the small rebound additive data in here

114
00:09:45.879 --> 00:09:49.419
so we can see that rebound.

115
00:09:49.419 --> 00:09:54.419
If we now compile, save, jump back into the mat and play,

116
00:09:54.419 --> 00:09:59.419
you should see that this is a pretty realistic run and jump.

117
00:09:59.419 --> 00:10:03.419
In the next video, we're going to look at how we can trigger an animation

118
00:10:03.419 --> 00:10:06.419
to be played from a keyboard input.
